From: Kevin Liu <11365056+kliu128@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: do not send WMI while the firmware restarts

After a firmware crash ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash() clears the HAL
rings and then drops ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH before the copy engine pipes
exist again. A WMI command sent in that window (hostapd reads the channel
survey every few seconds, which sends WMI_PDEV_BSS_CHAN_INFO_REQUEST)
reaches ath11k_ce_send() with a cleared ring and dereferences a NULL
pointer in ath11k_hal_srng_access_begin().

Keep the flag set until ath11k_ce_init_pipes() has run, and do not ask the
firmware for the channel survey unless the radio is up.

Signed-off-by: Kevin Liu <11365056+kliu128@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2431,6 +2431,12 @@
 		ath11k_err(ab, "failed to initialize CE: %d\n", ret);
 		goto err_firmware_stop;
 	}
+
+	/*
+	 * On the recovery path the copy engine rings were cleared and exist
+	 * again only from here on. Keep rejecting sends until then.
+	 */
+	clear_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ab->dev_flags);
 
 	ret = ath11k_dp_alloc(ab);
 	if (ret) {
@@ -2499,8 +2505,6 @@
 
 	ab->free_vdev_map = (1LL << (ab->num_radios * TARGET_NUM_VDEVS(ab))) - 1;
 
-	clear_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ab->dev_flags);
-
 	ret = ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready(ab);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_hal_srng_deinit;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -9336,6 +9336,11 @@
 	    ar->rx_channel != channel)
 		return;
 
+	/* no WMI while the firmware is being restarted */
+	if (ar->state != ATH11K_STATE_ON ||
+	    test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_RECOVERY, &ar->ab->dev_flags))
+		return;
+
 	if (ar->scan.state != ATH11K_SCAN_IDLE) {
 		ath11k_dbg(ar->ab, ATH11K_DBG_MAC,
 			   "ignoring bss chan info req while scanning..\n");
